    "title": "Why Spider-Man Is Fighting The Hand In Brand New Day",
    "text": "It's just been confirmed that Spider-Man: Brand New Day will see Tom Holland's Peter Parker fighting none other than The Hand. A sinister ninja clan operating in New York City, The Hand will be featured as a major threat among several villains in the MCU's fourth Spider-Man movie. The first trailer for Spider-Man: Brand New Day has just been released, confirming that the upcoming movie will be a street-level epic as Peter Parker grapples with his more isolated status quo four years afer Spider-Man: No Way Home while also dealing with dramatic changes to his powers amid rising threats in New York. With that in mind, here's what we know about The Hand and why they'll be fighting Spider-Man in Brand New Day. The new Spider-Man: Brand New Day trailer footage makes one thing perfectly clear: Peter Parker is in for one of his most exciting and chaotic adventures yet. Clashing with multiple classic foes, the Spider-Man: Brand New Day trailer features new looks at Mac Gargan's Scorpion (returning after a 9-year absence), Boomerang, and Tarantula, an impressive gauntlet of street-level threats. While not featured in the trailer, the major crime boss Tombstone is also expected to make an appearance as well. Brand New Day will also feature appearances from Bruce Banner's Hulk, The Punisher, and the heavily speculated MCU debut of Sadie Sink as Jean Grey (likely the figure wearing the yellow hood in the trailer). Not only is there a shot of Spider-Man unmasked fighting the Hand in what looks to be a prison, but there's another epic slow motion shot that sees the Webslinger in the air between buildings, leaping directly at a full force of the ninja warriors. All that said, one has to wonder why Spider-Man is fighting the Hand in the first place. A Brief History Of The Hand Explained (Why Is Spider-Man Fighting Them?) Adapted from their origins in the comics, The Hand is a global, centuries-old ninja criminal organization deeply tied to mysticism, resurrection rituals, and supernatural warfare. Given their established history, The Hand's role in Spider-Man: Brand New Day suggests something bigger is unfolding in New York, which would tie into the film's official synopsis, confirming that Peter Parker will uncover \"a new pattern of crimes that gives rise to one of the most powerful threats Spider-Man has ever faced.\" While Spider-Man doesn't have a history with The Hand, it's worth noting that Frank Castle's Punisher does. As a result, an uneasy team-up between Frank Castle and Peter Parker against The Hand does feel likely. Furthermore, there's honestly no better threat to justify the Daredevil/Spider-Man team up in the MCU fans have desperately been wanting for years (though Daredevil has yet to be confirmed for Brand New Day). Either way, The Hand's involvement in Spider-Man: Brand New Day truly is the perfect way to maintain high stakes with more street-level MCU storytelling, especially when you have a hero as powerful as Spider-Man. Release Date July 31, 2026 Director Destin Daniel Cretton Writers Chris McKenna, Erik Sommers, Steve Ditko, Stan Lee",
